WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.249
Accurate documentation is an essential part of blood culture collection, and every field earns its place.

2
00:00:06.249 --> 00:00:13.280
The date and time of collection, which fixes the sample against the fever curve and the antibiotic timeline.

3
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:21.092
The site from which the sample was obtained, which lets a positive catheter set be compared against a peripheral one.

4
00:00:21.092 --> 00:00:28.513
The number of sets collected, which tells the laboratory and the clinician how to read a single positive bottle.

5
00:00:28.513 --> 00:00:32.419
The volume obtained, which is the main determinant of yield.

6
00:00:32.419 --> 00:00:34.762
The patient's response to the procedure.

7
00:00:34.762 --> 00:00:41.012
And whether antibiotics were given before collection, which determines whether a negative result can be trusted.

